.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-ZFS-BOOKMARKS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-zfs-bookmarks
.Nd put the mounted data datasets in the Files sidebar at login
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The root file system's places already appear in the Files sidebar; a
second pool's datasets do not.
At each graphical login,
.Nm
finds every mounted ZFS file system whose mount point is not a system
directory or under
.Pa /home ,
and writes one bookmark for each, labelled with the last part of its
mount point, into the user's GTK bookmarks file, between two marker lines
it owns.
Everything else in the file is left as it was.
The file changes only when the set of datasets does.
It runs as the user and changes nothing else.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
The bookmarks.
.It Pa /etc/xdg/autostart/kldload-zfs-bookmarks.desktop
What runs it at login.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0; non-zero only on an unexpected error, with the line.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
GTK's bookmarks file has no comment syntax: each line is an address and a
label, and the two marker lines are read as lines like any other.
How the Files sidebar shows them, and whether they survive the file
being rewritten when the user adds a bookmark, has not been checked.
.Pp
On a desktop installed on 2026-08-30 the autostart entry was missing, so
it never ran.
